# Agent-runtime state. NOT project files — machine-local scratch written by the
# agent tooling, swept in once by a careless `git add -A`.
#
# .claude/worktrees/ is the one that actually breaks things: each entry is its
# own git repository, so committing it records a SUBMODULE (mode 160000)
# pointing at a commit no remote has. Anyone cloning this public repo gets a
# broken checkout for a directory that was never meant to leave this machine.
#
# .claude/ itself stays TRACKED — agents/, rules/ and skills/ are the project's
# operating manual and belong in the repo.
.claude-flow/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/proven-config.json
.claude/.proven-config-version

# Generated by `next dev` for AI tooling; not project instructions.
apps/web/AGENTS.md
apps/web/CLAUDE.md
